    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Land patents appeared in the 1850s, and by 1878 Bodcaw had a post office and stagecoach stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bodcaw%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1890, Bodcaw hosted businesses, industries, and the Bodcaw Academy, a Baptist school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bodcaw%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 1915 tornado damaged the Bodcaw Academy, and it was never rebuilt.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bodcaw%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "After the post office closed in 1959, Bodcaw incorporated in 1969 to offer local services.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bodcaw%2C_Arkansas"
    },
